---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-26-cross-links-and-species-pages.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-26',
  title: 'Cross-links between the Bring What You Already Have pages, and a line on every species page',
  tags: ['workflows', 'bring-what-you-have', 'internal-linking', 'species-pages'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 26, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Connected the Bring What You Already Have pages to each other and added a Bring What You Already
    Have card to the feature list on each of the nine species pages.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Pages updated</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><a href="/workflows/bring-what-you-have" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/bring-what-you-have</a>: the four routes now link to Import Records With Scout, Contracts &amp; E-Signatures and Applications &amp; Screening. The note on the existing Stripe account links to Payments &amp; Deposits, which is not a route.</li>
      <li><a href="/workflows/record-import" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/record-import</a>, <a href="/workflows/contracts-and-e-signatures" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/contracts-and-e-signatures</a> and <a href="/workflows/applications-and-screening" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/applications-and-screening</a>: a "Part of Bring What You Already Have" link back to the hub.</li>
      <li><a href="/workflows/client-portal" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/client-portal</a>: the card payment line links to Payments &amp; Deposits.</li>
      <li><a href="/" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">Homepage</a>: Payments &amp; Deposits added to the "Go deeper" links under the module grid.</li>
      <li>Species pages for dogs, cats, horses, goats, sheep, rabbits, alpacas, llamas and cattle: a Bring What You Already Have card in the feature list, linking to the hub. The card is left out of the in-page sticky navigation because it points off the page.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">SEO</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      Internal links only; no new pages. Every page in the cluster is now reachable from the hub and links back to it.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
